      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 3.15,
          "end": 7.75,
          "en": "-: Thus far, we always use the external template file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 8.889,
          "end": 11.178,
          "en": "and we haven't done anything regarding the styling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 11.178,
          "end": 12.228,
          "en": "of components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.228,
          "end": 13.41,
          "en": "Time to change both.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.41,
          "end": 17.34,
          "en": "Now, instead of using a external template file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.34,
          "end": 20.19,
          "en": "you can also use a inline template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.19,
          "end": 24.48,
          "en": "which means you define the HTML code in the TypeScript code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.48,
          "end": 25.62,
          "en": "Sounds strange.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.62,
          "end": 28.052,
          "en": "While it's possible, we can do this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.052,
          "end": 33,
          "en": "by simply going to our service component here, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33,
          "end": 37.14,
          "en": "And right now we point to this HTML file here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.14,
          "end": 40.59,
          "en": "Now we can change template URL to template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.59,
          "end": 42.9,
          "en": "One of the two has to be present either",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.9,
          "end": 44.5,
          "en": "a link to external template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.03,
          "end": 48.18,
          "en": "or just template to define it in this file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.18,
          "end": 50.7,
          "en": "But each component needs to have a template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.7,
          "end": 55.53,
          "en": "This is the one property you have to have at all times.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.53,
          "end": 58.62,
          "en": "So with that, now I changed to template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.62,
          "end": 61.83,
          "en": "Now we can write our template code here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.83,
          "end": 66.48,
          "en": "So here we could now replicate app server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.48,
          "end": 69.72,
          "en": "like this maybe twice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.72,
          "end": 70.93,
          "en": "We have to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.346,
          "end": 74.46000000000001,
          "en": "that we don't wrap this line because this is not supported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 76.226,
          "end": 77.776,
          "en": "in a default type script string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.776,
          "end": 80.199,
          "en": "And if I now save this, we see the same result as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.199,
          "end": 83.86,
          "en": "So it looks like nothing changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.86,
          "end": 85.136,
          "en": "And that is good in this case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.136,
          "end": 86.91,
          "en": "because we tried to make it look like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.91,
          "end": 89.366,
          "en": "But actually we did change the way we set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.366,
          "end": 91.17,
          "en": "up our template here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 91.17,
          "end": 95.46000000000001,
          "en": "Now we're defining the HTML code in this same file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 95.46000000000001,
          "end": 98.64,
          "en": "And actually, if you want to write multi-line strings here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 98.64,
          "end": 102.36,
          "en": "which you probably want, if you add more HTML code to it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 102.36,
          "end": 104.44,
          "en": "you can switch from a normal string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 105.566,
          "end": 108.16,
          "en": "with single quotation marks to using back ticks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 109.05,
          "end": 112.126,
          "en": "use JavaScript template expressions to be able to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 112.126,
          "end": 114.993,
          "en": "write model line strings in between there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 116.162,
          "end": 118.41,
          "en": "Now, so now between the opening and closing back tick",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 118.41,
          "end": 120.93,
          "en": "you may actually wrap the line",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 120.93,
          "end": 125.22,
          "en": "and now write your HTML code like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 125.22,
          "end": 127.126,
          "en": "What should you use?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 127.126,
          "end": 128.04,
          "en": "Should you use this approach here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 128.04,
          "end": 130.77,
          "en": "of using template or an external file?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 130.77,
          "end": 131.79,
          "en": "It depends.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 131.79,
          "end": 136.32,
          "en": "If you have not that much code, not that much HTML code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 136.32,
          "end": 139.05,
          "en": "Using an inline template like this might be fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 139.05,
          "end": 140.4,
          "en": "Then you have all the logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 141.378,
          "end": 143.7,
          "en": "of the TypeScript code and that is absolutely okay.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 143.7,
          "end": 146.5,
          "en": "But as soon as you have, let's say more than three lines",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 147.678,
          "end": 149.4,
          "en": "of code in the HTML part here in the template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 149.4,
          "end": 151.95,
          "en": "using an external file is a good idea to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 151.95,
          "end": 155.34,
          "en": "make it easier to follow and easier to understand.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 155.34,
          "end": 157.442,
          "en": "It is important though to keep in mind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 157.442,
          "end": 160.442,
          "en": "that you can use this approach that you can",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 160.442,
          "end": 164.07,
          "en": "in line your templates and very important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 164.07,
          "end": 168.39,
          "en": "that you need to have at least a template in a component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 168.39,
          "end": 171.39,
          "en": "You can omit the selector, you will later",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 171.39,
          "end": 173.59,
          "en": "in the routing section learn a different way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 174.686,
          "end": 176.16,
          "en": "of loading components without using their selector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 176.16,
          "end": 178.35,
          "en": "And you don't have to add styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 178.35,
          "end": 180.9,
          "en": "but templates have to be present.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 180.9,
          "end": 183.06,
          "en": "So that word templates.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 183.06,
          "end": 186.363,
          "en": "Now let's have a look at these styles in the next lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
